        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Michael Kanin, Ring Lardner Jr.\n- Products: Woman of the Year, When I Grow Up\n- Topics: Academy Awards, Hollywood blacklist, Red Scare\n\nFacts:\n- Michael Kanin was born on February 1, 1910, and he died on March 12, 1993.\n- Ring Lardner Jr. was born on August 19, 1915, and he died on October 31, 2000.\n- In 1942, Michael Kanin shared an Academy Award with Ring Lardner Jr. for writing the Katharine Hepburn-Spencer Tracy film comedy \"Woman of the Year.\"\n- Ring Lardner Jr. was an American journalist and screenwriter who was blacklisted by Hollywood movie studios during the Red Scare of the late 1940s and 1950s.\n- When I Grow Up is a 1951 American drama film written and directed by Michael Kanin.\n- Michael Kanin was an American director, producer, playwright, and screenwriter.",
